do_1 = "Implement proposed hyperfide command and cg alias with argument/JSON/exit parity and nonrecursive executable resolution."
do_2 = "Resolve approved release version/support window and public namespace ownership separately; never reserve or assume short alias/domain/package availability."
do_3 = "Take Makefile ownership after task25.3 and installer/release-script ownership after task26.1. Build and install an actual canonical hyperfide executable and the approved cg compatibility entrypoint from the same qualified linked implementation; a wrapper over an unbuilt or unrelated PATH executable is insufficient. Preserve all native component, libcurl and TLS link dependencies without duplicate standalone-main objects."
do_4 = "Update the actual installer, release and uninstaller paths to consume the approved canonical artifact manifest and install/remove both declared command names safely. Existing scripts/release.sh hardcodes strip/publish cg and overrides LDLIBS with legacy static flags; preserve the qualified link contract and explicitly package any required runtime libraries rather than silently dropping the new transport. Namespace and publication destinations remain configuration, never invented ownership. The release is relocatable, so its ELF files keep the host dynamic loader and RUNPATH $ORIGIN-relative bundled libraries; glibc's own members (the loader, libc, libm, libmvec, libpthread, libdl, librt, libutil, libresolv, libanl, libnsl, libBrokenLocale, libc_malloc_debug, libthread_db and libnss_*) are never bundled, because a bundled libc loaded by a host loader from a different glibc build crashes every runtime (observed on release 0d03ef51: glibc 2.43 bundle on a glibc 2.39 host, exit 139). Supported hosts need a glibc no older than the build host's, and release construction fails if a glibc member is staged or if the staged node does not report its pinned version both plainly and under the bundled library path."
do_5 = "Qualify clean remote builds, installation to a disposable prefix, both command names, argument/JSON/exit parity and uninstall against the real produced artifacts. Run documented release construction in a nonpublishing fixture; this task does not independently authorize production publication."
do_6 = "Implement the task's registered positive/negative assertions and immutable manifest; execute them remotely after approval, preserving command, exact revisions, complete artifacts and independent observed outcomes."

