do_1 = "Nothing in src calls AuthorityStore.activate; it is only reachable through storage.authority.v1 (durability.ts:283-285, :302) and every ordinary service refuses until an epoch exists (durability.ts:276-279). Add a trusted operator activation entry that drives activateInternal (durability.ts:200-239) once, BOOTSTRAP when there is no predecessor (:236)."
do_2 = "FileExternalAuthorityJournal requires uid ownership of its dir and file (authority_journal.ts:86, :96), mints a fresh randomUUID epoch per journal (:159) and publishCommitted needs a matching PENDING entry (:174); with three unit uids only one journal can hold the committed epoch, so the other roles fail assertExternalAuthorityCurrent (durability.ts:172-182). Add a follower path that adopts a committed epoch and proof_digest from the activating journal, verified, without minting."
do_3 = "Keep the LIVE_PROVIDER-only fence (fencing.ts:210) and the receipt checks with the 30 s expiry bound (durability.ts:226-229); do not accept the component-fixture fencer used by tests/hyperfide/support/identity_fixture.py:53-58 outside tests."
do_4 = "Replace the hardcoded authority_activated:false in deploy/hyperfide/migrate.mjs:54, :57, :66 and install-service.mjs:110, :116 with a store read."
do_5 = "Implement the task's registered positive/negative assertions and immutable manifest; execute them remotely after approval, preserving command, exact revisions, complete artifacts and independent observed outcomes."

